roduced or not and we  know th17 produce  il22 antibody il22 cytokine  so we need to do a il22 elispot assay  in this case the wells would be coated  with il-22  and the il-22 antibody and  we would detect the presence of il-22 in  the sample  now it has been seen in from this result  the candida infected  individual and his serum has a hell lot  of spots  developed in ali spot assay that means  his syrup  indeed has cells which are  producing il-22 cytokines  now we can also use this to determine  viral titers for example  in case of viral infections we have  th1 production production th1 some type  of t cell production  this th one type of cells are actually  inflammatory  so in order to understand the presence  of th1 sample th1 cells  in a patient sample who was infected by  a virus we can perform  several acids one is elispot acid so we  can  perform ifn gamma elispot assay because  we know that th1 cells whenever it is  produced they secretes ifn gamma or  interferon gamma  so detecting the presence of interferon  gamma would indirectly tell us about the  presence of  th1 cell so that is why whenever we do  the alispot assay if we see spots that  means  that patient that patient was infected  by the virus and now  th1 cells are produced as an immune  response so type of  immune response which type of cells are  produced in the immune response  if you want to analyze these kind of  questions elispot assay is one of the  best acid  now overall we can also compare that how  much an individual is  in how much the individual has started  an immune response against a viral  infection so here are two individuals we  can see the individual on the left hand  side  has more spots in the elispot assay that  means  strong immune response has been  generated in person one  compared to person two and that is why  we see more cytokine producing th  one type of cells in this example so  these kind of comparative analysis can  also be done  using elispot asset data so just to  summarize  the advantages of elispot assay that  single cell versus bulk analysis can be  done  individual cell variation is  biologically important and that can be  done  here elispot assay is extremely  extremely sensitive so you really  need very less amount of sample which is  important in a clinical setting now  elispot assay also allows a quantitative  measurement that is very important  elispot acid also reduce the sample  necessity that means in in case many  cases we don't get that much of sample  but as this assay is very sensitive so  it  i mean it doesn't require a whole lot of  sample so those are the advantages  of elispot assay and by the way elispot  assay is also cost effective and widely  used in the medical community for  these kind of purposes and specially  this is preferred by the immunologist to  determine what type of cells  are present when a particular type of  immune response is  augmented so i hope you enjoyed this  video if you like this video give it a  big thumbs up and don't forget to like  share and subscribe thank you
 

